    "scientific_verdict": "Across k in {1, 2, 3} oracle calls on D = 5, F_D^{sigma_l} Pi_m = Pi_{m^{-1}} F_D^{sigma_l} holds for all units m in Z_D^*. At k = 1, the full affine group Z_D rtimes Z_D^* preserves the unordered Born distribution. At k >= 2, involutive units (m^2 == 1 mod D) commute with F_D^{+-1} and preserve the k-call physics, whereas non-involutive units (m^2 != 1 mod D) and cyclic shifts (b != 0 mod D) break unitary equivalence while preserving |V_epsilon(f)|, and alternating (m, m^{-1}) calls restores exact intertwining for all m in Z_D^*."
  },
  "theorems": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "name": "Exact Dilation Intertwining and Involutive Covariance (m^2 == 1 mod D)",
      "statement": "For any unit m in Z_D^*, F_D^(sigma_l) Pi_m = Pi_(m^(-1)) F_D^(sigma_l). Whenever m^2 == 1 mod D, Pi_m commutes with F_D^(+-1), so |Psi_(epsilon, sigma)(y^(m))> = Pi_m |Psi_(epsilon, sigma)(y)> and P(x | y^(m)) = P((m^(-1) x) mod D | y) for all k >= 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "name": "Alternating (m, m^(-1)) Intertwining Rescue vs Uniform-Dilation Symmetry Breaking at k >= 2",
      "statement": "For any unit m in Z_D^*, alternating y^(m) on odd calls and y^(m^(-1)) on even calls maps |Psi(y)> to Pi_m |Psi(y)> (odd k) or Pi_(m^(-1)) |Psi(y)> (even k), whereas uniform dilation y^(m) with m^2 != 1 mod D at k >= 2 scales internal bilinear phases by m^(-2) != 1 mod D while preserving |V_epsilon(f^(m))| = |V_epsilon(f)|."
    },
    {
      "id": "T3",
      "name": "k = 1 Cyclic Word-Translation Invariance vs k >= 2 Internal Ramp Breaking",
      "statement": "Under cyclic word translation y^[+b]_w = y_((w + b) mod D), at k = 1 the Born distribution P_(epsilon_1, sigma_1)(x | y^[+b]) = P_(epsilon_1, sigma_1)(x | y) is invariant for all b in Z_D, whereas at k >= 2 internal phase ramps break translation invariance while preserving |V_epsilon(f^[+b])| = |V_epsilon(f)|."
    }
  ],
  "title": "Native Higher-Call Word-Permutation Covariance Audit: Involutive Dilation Invariance, m^2 != 1 Bilinear Symmetry Breaking at k >= 2, and Alternating Intertwining Rescue"
